     Collection +0x40 heap entries; +0x50 count; +0x54 capacity; +0x60 threshold;
     +0x64 recursion depth.
     Entry +0x20 heap callback object; +0x30 enabled/storage state; stride 0x40.
     Callback object +0x00 exact typed vtable; virtual +0x30 is the compactability predicate.
   
   Special Cases:
     uVar4 is the selected FCallbackEntry_Partial pointer and plVar5 is the selected
     FWeakCallbackObject_Partial pointer. They are register-only projections and cannot be
     safely retyped through the local-variable API.
     local_res* values are decompiler stack/register phantoms.
   
   Rollback Relevance:
     Broadcast owns topology maintenance as well as subscriber execution. Suppressing a hub
     virtual skips stale-listener cleanup; replaying later compacts the confirmation-time graph.
   
   Source:
     SoulcaliburVI.exe .text 0x140399DF0 and registration/post-broadcast callers. */

